---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import config from '../data/config.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy & Local Architecture — Lirune Reader"
  description="Lirune Reader's strict offline-first privacy architecture: zero telemetry, zero analytics, local database storage, and zero internet permissions on Android."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <div class="site-container site-container--narrow section-spacing">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="badge badge-success">Privacy Architecture</span>
      <h1>Privacy & Data Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-subtitle">Effective Date: October 2026. Lirune is built on a simple commitment: <strong>what you read belongs strictly to you</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="privacy-content-card surface-card">
      <section class="privacy-section-block">
        <h2>1. The Zero-Telemetry Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          Lirune Reader does not collect, record, transmit, or monetize any personal information, telemetry, usage metrics, or reading habits.
        </p>
        <ul class="privacy-bullets" role="list">
          <li><strong>No Analytics SDKs:</strong> There are no Google Analytics, Firebase Analytics, Mixpanel, or third-party trackers bundled in the application.</li>
          <li><strong>No Crash Telemetry:</strong> Crash traces are not silently transmitted across the network. If an unhandled exception occurs, errors are logged solely to local files on your machine.</li>
          <li><strong>No Reading Timers or Telemetry:</strong> How fast you read, what pages you stop on, and how long you spend on a chapter is never logged or transmitted.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section-block">
        <h2>2. Local Document Indexation & Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Your digital documents (EPUB, PDF, CBZ, FB2, MOBI, etc.) remain strictly on your local filesystem:
        </p>
        <ul class="privacy-bullets" role="list">
          <li><strong>Local SQLite Database:</strong> Library records, reading progress, bookmarks, and user highlights are stored in a standard SQLite database residing in your user profile directory.</li>
          <li><strong>No Remote Accounts:</strong> You do not need to create an account, log in with an email, or connect a social profile to use Lirune.</li>
          <li><strong>No Cloud Lock-in:</strong> Lirune does not force your files into a remote cloud. If you wish to back up your library, you can simply back up your local folder or sync it via Syncthing, Nextcloud, or OneDrive on your own terms.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section-block">
        <h2>3. Android Permissions & Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          On Android, privacy is enforced at the operating system manifest level:
        </p>
        <ul class="privacy-bullets" role="list">
          <li><strong>Stripped Network Permission:</strong> The production release APK explicitly strips <code>android.permission.INTERNET</code>. The operating system sandbox prevents the app from creating sockets or opening HTTP connections.</li>
          <li><strong>Storage Access Framework (SAF):</strong> Lirune does not request broad legacy "All Files Access" permissions. You grant access specifically to the directory you choose using Android's native system file picker.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section-block">
        <h2>4. Open Source Verification</h2>
        <p>
          Lirune's privacy guarantees are not just a marketing claim—they are publicly verifiable. The entire source code for both Windows and Android runtimes is open source under the <strong>GNU General Public License v3.0</strong> on GitHub.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are welcome to audit network requests using tools like Wireshark or Fiddler, inspect the source code, or compile the binaries yourself from the public repository.
        </p>
        <div class="privacy-action-row">
          <a href={config.githubRepo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-secondary">
            <span>Inspect Source on GitHub ↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .privacy-content-card {
    padding: clamp(28px, 5vw, 48px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-8);
  }

  .privacy-section-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
  }

  .privacy-section-block h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .privacy-section-block p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .privacy-bullets {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding-left: 4px;
  }

  .privacy-bullets li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 20px;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .privacy-bullets li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 4px;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--status-success);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .privacy-bullets strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .privacy-action-row {
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }
</style>
